alphaCertified -- certify a list of numerical solutions via alphaCertified
**************************************************************************

Description
===========

For a given polynomial system and a list of numerical roots, this function
certifies roots using a software "alphaCertified" (see
https://www.math.tamu.edu/~sottile/research/stories/alphaCertified/ ).

In order to use alphaCertified, users need to let the package knows a directory
for alphaCertified when it is loaded.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage("NumericalCertification", Configuration =>                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = NumericalCertification                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Package                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{"ALPHACERTIFIEDexec" => "some/path/to/alphaCertified"})                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Function only takes elements over *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR, or *note CC:
(Macaulay2Doc)CC, as an input.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = CC[x1,x2,y1,y2];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = polySystem {3*y1 + 2*y2 -1, 3*x1 + 2*x2 -3.5, x1^2 + y1^2 -1, x2^2 +|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|y2^2 -1};                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : p1 = point{{.95, .32, -.30, .95}};                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : p2 = point{{.65,.77,.76,-.64}};                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : P = {p1, p2};                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The function can be used as alphaCertified(f,p). It generates output files via
the software alphaCertified. The output can be found in the user's directory of
alphaCertified.

Users can also apply options for alphaCertified (e.g. alphaCertified(f, P,
PRECISION => 4096)). For possible options for alphaCertified, see
"alphaCertified manual" (see
https://www.math.tamu.edu/~sottile/research/stories/alphaCertified/Download/V13
/alphaCertified.pdf ).









Ways to use alphaCertified:
===========================

  * "alphaCertified(PolySystem,List)"

