CertificationOptions -- options for certification method
********************************************************

Description
===========

This is an option for *note certifySingularSolution: certifySingularSolution,
and *note certifySolutions: certifySolutions,. There are three possible options
alphaTheory, intervalArithmetic and alphaCertified. By default, it takes alpha
theory as a strategy.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = RR[x1,x2,y1,y2];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = polySystem {3*y1 + 2*y2 -1, 3*x1 + 2*x2 -7/2,x1^2 + y1^2 -1, x2^2 + |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|y2^2 - 1};                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : p = point {{.95437, .318445, -.298627, .947941}};                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : peek certifySolutions(f, {p})                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = MutableHashTable{alphaValues => {1.04693e-10}}                          |
|                      certifiedDistinct => {p}                               |
|                      certifiedReal => {p}                                   |
|                      certifiedRegular => {p}                                |
|                      certifiedSingular => {}                                |
|                      nonCertified => {}                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : peek certifySolutions(f, {p}, Strategy => "intervalArithmetic")         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = MutableHashTable{certifiedReal => {|  [.954349,.95439] + [0,-0]*ii      |
|                      certifiedRegular => {|  [.954349,.95439] + [0,-0]*     |
|                      certifiedSingular => {}                                |
|                      nonCertified => {}                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|[.318414,.318476] + [0,-0]*ii [-.298641,-.298614] + [0,-0]*ii                |
|ii [.318414,.318476] + [0,-0]*ii [-.298641,-.298614] + [0,-0]*               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|[.94792,.947962] + [0,-0]*ii |}   }                                          |
|ii [.94792,.947962] + [0,-0]*ii |}                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

