computeConstants -- compute the square of the auxiliary quantities related to alpha theory
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (alpha, beta, gamma) = computeConstants(PS, P)
  * Inputs:
      * PS, a *note polynomial system: (NAGtypes)PolySystem,, 
      * P, a *note point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, 

Description
===========

alpha theory uses three auxiliary quantities related to the input polynomial
system and point.

Beta value is defined by the length of the Newton step and gamma value is the
quantity which is inversely proportional to the length between exact solution
and the given point.

Alpha value is defined by the multiplication of beta and gamma. When it is
smaller than  $0.157671$, then the input point is an approximate solution to
the system. The function *note certifyRegularSolution: certifyRegularSolution,
does this process.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = RR[x1,x2,y1,y2];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = polySystem {3*y1 + 2*y2 -1, 3*x1 + 2*x2 -3.5,x1^2 + y1^2 -1, x2^2 + |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|y2^2 - 1};                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : p = point{{.95,.32,-.30,.95}};                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (a, b, g) = computeConstants(f,p)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = (.00621269, .0000277104, 224.2)                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use computeConstants:
=============================

  * "computeConstants(PolySystem,AbstractPoint)"
  * "computeConstants(PolySystem,Matrix)"

